## F. Dual-mode security review

Split auth review into **two explicit modes**. Diff-only “does this route call the guard?” misses composition bugs (bootstrap + primitive allow-all was one example).

| Mode | Question | When to run |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Route compliance** | Does every new/changed handler call the correct guard (`requireSessionPermission`, `requirePlatformMaintainer`, `requireAlliancePermission`, explicit `hqUserId` check)? | Every PR touching `src/app/api/**` |
| **Auth architecture** | Can any **session shape** reach a handler despite the guard? Trace mint → bind → primitive → handler. | Auth/RBAC/session PRs; **any** change to `context.ts`, bootstrap, connect, middleware; periodic audit of `main` |

### Real Steel

On auth-touching PRs, at least one pass must run **Auth architecture** mode using sections **A** and **C** above. Route compliance alone is insufficient for `real-steel-ready` when the PR touches `src/lib/rbac/**`, `src/lib/session/**`, or `/api/admin/**`.

### `/review-security` Custom Instructions

When launching the security-review subagent on this repo, include **Auth architecture** unless the PR is docs-only:

```text
Custom Instructions: Alliance HQ auth architecture pass per .cursor/rules/auth-boundary-review.mdc:
(1) Permission primitive pass — sessionHasPermission / sessionHasPermissionForAlliance; no allow on hqUserId null; flag return true in rbac/.
(2) Trace session mint paths (bootstrap, getOrCreateSession) to privileged routes in the diff.
(3) Confirm negative e2e exists or is required for new admin/privilege surfaces (bootstrap cookie → 403).
(4) Flag unit tests that assert permissive auth for hqUserId null.
```

For non-auth PRs, route compliance mode is enough:

```text
Custom Instructions: Route compliance only — verify new/changed API handlers call requireSessionPermission or equivalent; tenant scope by alliance id.
```

